// Consul, comprehensively: servirtium-vcr's pre-recorded/from-testcontainers
// "Pattern for comprehensive suites" (README) applied to HashiCorp Consul
// 1.15 (1.15.10, BSL 1.1: BOUND, so every tape starts with its
// LICENSE NOTICE), after the CouchDB pilot.
//
// Two describe blocks, two sets of tapes:
//
// 1. "modules/consul": ported from testcontainers-go modules/consul/consul_test.go
//    (by way of testcontainers-ae). It tests the MODULE (default start, the
//    config string and config file options): four tapes, one container each,
//    ACLs off, the original representative cases.
//
// 2. "Consul HTTP API": written for servirtium-vcr. Re-usable recordings of
//    Consul's HTTP API, one tape per scenario, for any language's tests to
//    replay with no Consul. This is the comprehensive part. Component-level
//    tests of Consul's API, never "end-to-end": the tapes stand in for Consul.
//    Its agent runs with ACLs ENABLED and default policy "deny", so that
//    there is a login.
//
// PORTING: this file is the reference for what each tape holds; the tapes are
// the re-usable part. A port is a test in your language and test framework
// that makes the same requests in the same order against a Servirtium replay
// server loaded with the tape, and checks the same things. Every request is
// plain HTTP/1.1 with these headers and no others:
//   User-Agent: testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)
//   Content-Type: application/json   (a JSON body; text/plain for a KV value)
//   X-Consul-Token: ...              (every logged-in request, see below)
// Playback is strict about method, path (query string included, exactly as
// written here, parameters in this order), the recorded request headers and
// the body (byte for byte: send the JSON bodies exactly as written in this
// file, no spaces), and fails a case whose recorded requests are not all
// made. Host, Connection and Content-Length are on the tapes but are
// transport headers, not compared. Consul's JSON is indented four spaces and
// its errors are plain text, not JSON: don't parse an error body.
//
// Login, and "already logged in"
// ------------------------------
// Consul's credential is an ACL token (X-Consul-Token). The agent starts with
// ACLs on and no token: nothing but the public status endpoints works, and
// "logging in" is the one-time ACL BOOTSTRAP, PUT /v1/acl/bootstrap, which
// mints the global-management token (a second bootstrap is refused). That is
// the login tape, bootstraps_the_acl_system: anonymous 403s, the bootstrap,
// the refused second bootstrap, and who-am-I with the new token. It runs on
// its own container (a container can be bootstrapped once). Every other case
// is ALREADY LOGGED IN: each request carries a management token the live test
// obtained by bootstrapping the shared container outside the recorder
// (login_live below), and the bootstrap is not on that case's tape. Two cases
// also use a second, limited token they create on the tape (the policy and
// token cases). Consul's other login, PUT /v1/acl/login against an auth
// method (JWT, OIDC, Kubernetes), needs an identity provider: out of scope.
//
// PORTING, getting into the logged-in state without the login tape: send any
// `X-Consul-Token: <anything>` header on every request. The tapes hold the
// token as X_CONSUL_TOKEN_N (Servirtium's redact_credential_header preset)
// and playback matches a credential header on PRESENCE, not value. A
// consequence: a replay cannot tell a good token from a forged one, so the
// cases that show a refusal for a missing token send no header at all, and
// the one that shows an unknown token (refuses_an_anonymous_or_unknown_token)
// records Consul's 403 for it but replays against any header. The token's
// SecretID is tokenized wherever it appears (the bootstrap response, the
// token/self response), as the same X_CONSUL_TOKEN_N.
//
// What varies between runs, and what the tapes do with it
// --------------------------------------------------------
// Every rule is registered in api_rules() below, with its reason; the
// "## [Recording rules]" table at the end of each tape lists them and the
// interactions each touched. In short:
//   - normalized ({{uuid-N}}, the same token wherever the value recurs,
//     because a client sends it back): every uuid (node id, session ids, ACL
//     policy ids and token accessors) except Consul's built-in
//     00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000000N ids, which are stable.
//   - collapsed (one constant): Raft indexes (CreateIndex and ModifyIndex in
//     every body, the X-Consul-Index header, a cas or Index a client sends
//     back, the "reset index" of a refused bootstrap) all become 1, and
//     times. PORTING: an index is opaque. Read the one you are given and send
//     it back; never assert that one is larger than another, or its value
//     (on a replay each is 1). cas=0, "create only if absent", is a different
//     thing and is left as 0.
//   - redacted: the token header and the secrets it holds, X_CONSUL_TOKEN_N.
//   - left out: Date.
//   - a "Hash" (base64 SHA-256 Consul puts on tokens and policies, to detect
//     change: a token's covers its random ids and times) is collapsed too.
// Deterministic values are left alone: the node's name (the config sets
// "tcae-node"), keys, values, flags, LockIndex.
//
// Awkward points
// --------------
// Consul orders the members of a list that is not sorted by name (sessions,
// say) in no stable way across runs, so the cases that list hold at most one
// of them, or have a stable sort (keys, services, checks by id). An opt-in
// stable-ordering feature in Servirtium's core would let a case list more.
// The node name, agent/self and the metrics endpoints are not in the API
// cases: agent/self is a dump of the host's configuration (cpu counts,
// paths) and the module cases above already record it.
//
// In and out of scope
// -------------------
// In: the ACL bootstrap and token/policy lifecycle and their enforcement; the
// public status endpoints and the datacenter, node and member lists; KV
// (put, get, raw, flags, keys, separator, recurse, cas, delete, cas delete)
// and transactions; sessions and locks (acquire, release, renew, destroy,
// delete behaviour); agent services and TTL checks (register, pass, warn,
// fail, deregister), the health and catalog views of them, and external-node
// registration through the catalog; the representative errors 400, 403, 404,
// 405 and 500 (Consul answers a few bad inputs with 500).
// Out: blocking queries and watches (?index=&wait=: timing), the event API,
// prepared queries, config entries and Connect (service mesh), DNS (UDP/TCP
// 8600), snapshots (binary), the operator/raft and autopilot endpoints
// (node specific), gossip and WAN federation (one node), coordinates, the ACL
// auth-method login and replication, and the UI. Each could be a later case.
//
// Running it (from pre-recorded/from-testcontainers):
//   ae test consul/test_consul.ae                         container, no Servirtium
//   TCAE_VCR=record   ae test consul/test_consul.ae       write the tapes
//   TCAE_VCR=check    ae test consul/test_consul.ae       fail if a tape changed
//   TCAE_VCR=playback ae test consul/test_consul.ae       no container: the tapes
// The API cases share one container (started on the first one and removed at
// the end); the login case and the module cases each start their own.

import std.spec
import std.string
import std.http.client
import std.json
import testcontainers as tc
import testcontainers.docker
import testcontainers.testing
import servirtium
import modules.consul

const IMAGE = "hashicorp/consul:1.15"

// The User-Agent this test's HTTP client sends, as an app's client library
// would: Go's net/http adds `Go-http-client/1.1` by itself, Aether's
// std.http.client adds none. Set here, in the test's own client, so the
// recordings show a representative request; Servirtium records what the
// client sends and adds nothing of its own.
const USER_AGENT = "testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)"

// The token the logged-in cases send in playback, where there is no Consul to
// bootstrap. Any value does: the tapes match X-Consul-Token on presence.
const PLAYBACK_TOKEN = "any-value-replay-matches-on-presence"

// The agent the API cases run: a named node (so the name is the same every
// run) with ACLs on and everything denied until a token says otherwise.
const API_CONFIG = "{ \"server\":true, \"node_name\":\"tcae-node\", \"acl\":{ \"enabled\":true, \"default_policy\":\"deny\" } }"

// (status, body, error) for a request with an optional JSON/plain body.
fn call_api(method: string, url: string, body: string) -> (int, string, string) {
    req = client.request(method, url)
    client.set_header(req, "User-Agent", USER_AGENT)
    client.set_timeout(req, 10s)
    if string.length(body) > 0 { client.set_body(req, string.bytes(body), "application/json") }
    r, err = client.send_request(req)
    client.request_free(req)
    if err != "" { return 0, "", err }
    status = client.response_status(r)
    out = client.response_body(r)
    client.response_free(r)
    return status, out, ""
}

// Wait for a leader election, which follows "agent running" by a moment
// (up to 10 s, a try every 100 ms).
fn leader(base: string) -> (string, string) {
    tries = 0
    last = ""
    while tries < 100 {
        st, body, err = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/status/leader", "")
        last = err
        if err == "" && st == 200 && string.length(body) > 4 { return body, "" }
        tries = tries + 1
        sleep(100)
    }
    return "", "no leader: ${last}"
}

// In a live run, wait for the leader against the container itself, before
// the recording starts: how many polls the election takes is timing, and a
// tape that recorded them would differ run to run. The case's own leader
// check then finds one at once, and the tape holds just that request.
fn await_leader(c: *docker.Container) {
    _ld, lerr = leader(agent_url(c))
    spec.assert_ok(lerr, "leader elected before recording")
}

fn node_name(base: string) -> string {
    st, body, err = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/agent/self", "")
    if err != "" || st != 200 { return "" }
    doc, perr = json.parse(body)
    if perr != "" { return "" }
    cfg, _ = json.object_get(doc, "Config")
    nn, _ = json.object_get(cfg, "NodeName")
    s, _ = json.get_string(nn)
    json.free(doc)
    return s
}

// The agent's base URL ("" in playback, where there is no container).
fn agent_url(c: *docker.Container) -> string {
    if c == null { return "" }
    hp, err = consul.api_endpoint(c)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "api endpoint")
    spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(hp, "localhost:") == 1, "host:port, no scheme: ${hp}")
    return "http://${hp}"
}

// Go's TestConsul body: API up, register / list / deregister a service; plus a leader and KV.
fn assert_consul_works(base: string, name: string) {
    ld, lerr = leader(base)
    spec.assert_ok(lerr, "leader elected")
    spec.assert_contains(ld, ":8300", "the leader is a server RPC address: ${ld}")

    st, _, perr = call_api("PUT", "${base}/v1/kv/tcae/greeting", "hello consul")
    spec.assert_ok(perr, "KV put")
    spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "KV put is 200")
    st2, raw, gerr = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/kv/tcae/greeting?raw", "")
    spec.assert_ok(gerr, "KV get")
    spec.assert_eq(st2, 200, "KV get is 200")
    spec.assert_str_eq(raw, "hello consul", "the value read back is the value put")

    reg = "{\"ID\":\"abcd\",\"Name\":\"${name}\"}"
    st3, _, rerr = call_api("PUT", "${base}/v1/agent/service/register", reg)
    spec.assert_ok(rerr, "register")
    spec.assert_eq(st3, 200, "register is 200")
    _, svcs, _ = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/agent/services", "")
    spec.assert_contains(svcs, "\"ID\": \"abcd\"", "the service is listed")
    spec.assert_contains(svcs, "\"Service\": \"${name}\"", "under the name we gave")
    st4, _, derr = call_api("PUT", "${base}/v1/agent/service/deregister/abcd", "")
    spec.assert_ok(derr, "deregister")
    spec.assert_eq(st4, 200, "deregister is 200")
    _, after, _ = call_api("GET", "${base}/v1/agent/services", "")
    spec.assert_true(string.contains(after, "\"abcd\"") == 0, "the service is gone")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The API cases: HTTP helpers
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

var api: string = ""
var tok: string = ""

// A string in a JSON body by a dotted path ("0.Key", "ID", "Results.1.KV.Key");
// "" when absent or not a string.
fn jstr(body: string, path: string) -> string {
    doc, err = json.parse(body)
    if err != "" { return "" }
    let v: ptr = doc
    rest = path
    while string.length(rest) > 0 && v != null {
        p = rest
        dot = string.index_of(rest, ".")
        if dot >= 0 {
            p = string.substring(rest, 0, dot)
            rest = string.substring(rest, dot + 1, string.length(rest))
        } else {
            rest = ""
        }
        if json.json_type(v) == json.JSON_ARRAY {
            idx, _ = string.to_int(p)
            a, _ = json.array_get(v, idx)
            v = a
        } else {
            o, _ = json.object_get(v, p)
            v = o
        }
    }
    out = ""
    if v != null {
        s, serr = json.get_string(v)
        if serr == "" { out = string.copy(s) }
    }
    json.free(doc)
    return out
}


// HCL for a policy, as the JSON string Consul takes: write ' for the double
// quotes HCL needs and this puts \" there, so the test source stays readable.
fn hcl(s: string) -> string {
    return string.replace_all(string.replace_all(s, "\n", "\\n"), "'", "\\\"")
}

// The digits that follow marker in body ("" when it is absent): a Raft index
// read out of a response, to send back as ?cas=.
fn num_after(body: string, marker: string) -> string {
    i = string.index_of(body, marker)
    if i < 0 { return "" }
    j = i + string.length(marker)
    out = ""
    while j < string.length(body) {
        ch = string.char_at(body, j)
        if ch < 48 || ch > 57 { return out }
        out = string.concat(out, string.from_char(ch))
        j = j + 1
    }
    return out
}

// A request: (status, body). ctype is the body's Content-Type (ignored when
// the body is empty); t "" sends no X-Consul-Token. A transport error fails
// the case.
fn http_send(method: string, url: string, t: string, ctype: string, body: string) -> (int, string, string) {
    req = client.request(method, url)
    client.set_header(req, "User-Agent", USER_AGENT)
    client.set_timeout(req, 30s)
    if string.length(t) > 0 { client.set_header(req, "X-Consul-Token", t) }
    if string.length(body) > 0 { client.set_body(req, string.bytes(body), ctype) }
    r, err = client.send_request(req)
    client.request_free(req)
    if err != "" { return 0, "", err }
    st = client.response_status(r)
    b = client.response_body(r)
    client.response_free(r)
    return st, b, ""
}

// A logged-in request with a JSON body (or none).
fn cv(method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    return cv_as(tok, method, path, body)
}

// The same with the given token ("" sends none).
fn cv_as(t: string, method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send(method, "${api}/v1/${path}", t, "application/json", body)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// A KV value: plain text.
fn kv_put(path: string, value: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send("PUT", "${api}/v1/${path}", tok, "text/plain", value)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "PUT ${path}")
    return st, b
}

fn anonymous(method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    return cv_as("", method, path, body)
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The live containers (record, check and off modes only)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

var shared_addr: string = ""
var shared_container: ptr = null
var shared_token: string = ""

// PUT /v1/acl/bootstrap until it answers (ACL setup follows the leader
// election by a moment): (status, body).
fn bootstrap_live(addr: string) -> (int, string) {
    tries = 0
    st = 0
    b = ""
    while tries < 100 {
        s2, b2, err = http_send("PUT", "${addr}/v1/acl/bootstrap", "", "application/json", "")
        if err == "" { st = s2; b = b2 }
        if err == "" && s2 == 200 { return s2, b2 }
        tries = tries + 1
        sleep(100)
    }
    return st, b
}

// The shared container's base URL, starting and bootstrapping it on first use
// ("" on failure). Sets shared_token to the management token.
fn shared() -> string {
    if string.length(shared_addr) > 0 { return shared_addr }
    c, err = consul.run(IMAGE) { config_string(API_CONFIG) }
    spec.assert_ok(err, "consul starts")
    if err != "" { return "" }
    shared_container = c as ptr
    a = agent_url(c)
    _ld, lerr = leader(a)
    spec.assert_ok(lerr, "leader elected")
    st, b = bootstrap_live(a)
    spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "bootstrap (not recorded): ${b}")
    if st != 200 { return "" }
    shared_token = jstr(b, "SecretID")
    shared_addr = a
    return shared_addr
}

// Start a logged-in API case: in a live mode, the shared container and, should
// an earlier failed run have left things, the case's keys, services and
// objects removed (cleanup lists "METHOD path" strings; none of it is
// recorded); then the recording. Sets `api` and `tok`; returns the recording
// handle, and ok = 0 when the case cannot run.
fn begin(case_: string, cleanup: string[]) -> (ptr, int) {
    addr = ""
    tok = PLAYBACK_TOKEN
    if servirtium.live() == 1 {
        addr = shared()
        if addr == "" { return null, 0 }
        tok = shared_token
        for step in cleanup {
            sp = string.index_of(step, " ")
            http_send(string.substring(step, 0, sp), "${addr}/v1/${string.substring(step, sp + 1, string.length(step))}", tok, "application/json", "")
        }
    }
    base, rec = servirtium.recording("consul", case_, addr)
    api = base
    return rec, 1
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Recording rules
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// The module cases' rules.
fn module_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // The licence terms of the recorded service, written at the top of each
    // tape (UPSTREAM-TERMS.md).
    servirtium.license_notice("Recorded against hashicorp/consul:1.15 (Consul 1.15.10), licensed under\nthe Business Source License 1.1 by HashiCorp. Its Additional Use Grant\ndoes not cover offering Consul to third parties in a hosted or embedded\nproduct that competes with HashiCorp's paid versions. Use of this tape\nis subject to those terms; see UPSTREAM-TERMS.md in servirtium-vcr's\npre-recorded/from-testcontainers.")
    // What differs run to run (and machine to machine): the Raft index
    // header, the node id, and the counters and host facts in
    // /v1/agent/self's Stats. X-Consul-Index stays on the tape (it is
    // Consul's own, part of its API), with its value collapsed: a number
    // still, since a client parses it as one.
    servirtium.collapse("X-Consul-Index: [0-9]+", "X-Consul-Index: 1")
    servirtium.normalize(servirtium.UUID, "node-id")
    for stat in ["applied_index", "commit_index", "last_log_index", "last_log_term", "term",
                 "last_contact", "fsm_pending", "goroutines", "cpu_count", "max_procs",
                 "event_queue", "event_time", "member_time", "query_time", "intent_queue",
                 "query_queue", "health_score", "coordinate_resets"] {
        servirtium.collapse("\"${stat}\": \"[0-9]+\"", "\"${stat}\": \"0\"")
    }
    servirtium.collapse("\"arch\": \"[a-z0-9_]+\"", "\"arch\": \"ARCH\"")

}

// The API cases' rules. Rules apply to every recording after them, so the two
// blocks each clear and register their own.
fn api_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // The licence terms of the recorded service (UPSTREAM-TERMS.md), again,
    // since clear_rules() dropped the module cases' notice.
    servirtium.license_notice("Recorded against hashicorp/consul:1.15 (Consul 1.15.10), licensed under\nthe Business Source License 1.1 by HashiCorp. Its Additional Use Grant\ndoes not cover offering Consul to third parties in a hosted or embedded\nproduct that competes with HashiCorp's paid versions. Use of this tape\nis subject to those terms; see UPSTREAM-TERMS.md in servirtium-vcr's\npre-recorded/from-testcontainers.")
    // The session credential. Registered FIRST: the preset writes each
    // distinct token as X_CONSUL_TOKEN_N in the header and, because a token
    // is 8+ characters, wherever else the same value appears (a bootstrap's
    // SecretID and ID, token/self's SecretID). Later rules only see the rest.
    servirtium.redact_credential_header("X-Consul-Token")
    // Raft indexes. Consul stamps every object with CreateIndex and
    // ModifyIndex and every response with X-Consul-Index; they count writes
    // since the container started, so they differ with any change to the
    // setup. A client sends one back as ?cas=N (and as "Index" in a txn), but
    // takes it from a response, so a constant works both ways: collapsed to 1
    // everywhere, replay returns 1 and the client sends 1. (Not LockIndex,
    // which counts a key's lock acquisitions: stable. Not cas=0, which means
    // "only if absent".)
    servirtium.collapse("X-Consul-Index: [0-9]+", "X-Consul-Index: 1")
    servirtium.collapse("(?<=\"CreateIndex\": |\"ModifyIndex\": )[0-9]+", "1")
    servirtium.collapse("(?<=cas=)[1-9][0-9]*", "1")
    servirtium.collapse("(?<=\"Index\":)[1-9][0-9]*", "1")
    servirtium.collapse("(?<=reset index: )[0-9]+", "1")
    // Every uuid: the node's id, session ids, ACL policy ids and token
    // accessors. A client sends them back (a session id in ?acquire=, a
    // policy id in a path), hence normalized, not collapsed. Consul's
    // built-in policies are 00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000000N: stable, and
    // clearer left as they are.
    servirtium.normalize(string.concat("(?!00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000000[0-9])", servirtium.UUID), "uuid")
    // The Hash of a token or policy: a token's covers its accessor, secret
    // and times, so it differs every run; nobody sends it back (a client's
    // change detection would use ModifyIndex or the Hash only as an opaque
    // ETag-like value). Collapsed for every object, the stable policy hashes
    // too, since a pattern cannot tell them apart.
    servirtium.collapse("(?<=\"Hash\": \")[A-Za-z0-9+/=]{44}(?=\")", "HASH")
    // Times: a token's or policy's CreateTime.
    servirtium.collapse(servirtium.RFC3339, "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

main() {
    fw = spec.init()
    if servirtium.skip_if_no_engine(fw) == 1 { return spec.run_summary(fw) }

    module_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "modules/consul") {
        spec.after_each() callback { testing.cleanup_all() }

        spec.it("serves the HTTP API (TestConsul/Default)") callback {
            let c: *docker.Container = null
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                c2, err = consul.run(IMAGE)
                testing.cleanup_container(c2)
                spec.assert_ok(err, "consul starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                c = c2
                await_leader(c)
            }
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("consul", "serves_the_http_api", agent_url(c))
            assert_consul_works(base, "Default")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        spec.it("takes a config string (TestConsul/WithConfigString)") callback {
            let c: *docker.Container = null
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                c2, err = consul.run(IMAGE) {
                    config_string("{ \"server\":true, \"node_name\":\"tcae-string-node\" }")
                }
                testing.cleanup_container(c2)
                spec.assert_ok(err, "consul starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                c = c2
                await_leader(c)
            }
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("consul", "takes_a_config_string", agent_url(c))
            assert_consul_works(base, "WithConfigString")
            spec.assert_str_eq(node_name(base), "tcae-string-node", "CONSUL_LOCAL_CONFIG reached the agent")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        spec.it("takes a config file (TestConsul/WithConfigFile)") callback {
            let c: *docker.Container = null
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                c2, err = consul.run(IMAGE) {
                    config_file("consul/testdata/node-name.json")
                }
                testing.cleanup_container(c2)
                spec.assert_ok(err, "consul starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                c = c2
                await_leader(c)
            }
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("consul", "takes_a_config_file", agent_url(c))
            assert_consul_works(base, "WithConfigFile")
            spec.assert_str_eq(node_name(base), "tcae-file-node", "the config file reached the agent")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        spec.it("starts with Go's testdata/config.json") callback {
            let c: *docker.Container = null
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                c2, err = consul.run(IMAGE) {
                    config_file("consul/testdata/config.json")
                }
                testing.cleanup_container(c2)
                spec.assert_ok(err, "consul starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                c = c2
                await_leader(c)
            }
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("consul", "starts_with_gos_testdata_config_json", agent_url(c))
            assert_consul_works(base, "GoConfig")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }
    }

    api_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "Consul HTTP API") {
        spec.after_each() callback { api = "" }

        // ---- the login tape ----------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: ACLs are on and nothing has a token yet, so "logging in" is
        // the one-time bootstrap. On its own container; no token on the first
        // requests.
        //   GET  /v1/status/leader              -> 200 "127.0.0.1:8300" (public)
        //   GET  /v1/acl/token/self             -> 403 "token does not exist: ACL not found" (plain text)
        //   GET  /v1/kv/tcae/hello              -> 403 "Permission denied: anonymous token lacks permission
        //                                          'key:read' on "tcae/hello". The anonymous token is ..."
        //   PUT  /v1/acl/bootstrap              -> 200 {"ID":..,"AccessorID":{{uuid-1}},"SecretID":..,
        //        "Description":"Bootstrap Token (Global Management)","Policies":[{"ID":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
        //        "Name":"global-management"}],...}; the SecretID (also in ID) is X_CONSUL_TOKEN_1
        //   PUT  /v1/acl/bootstrap              -> 403 "Permission denied: ACL bootstrap no longer allowed (reset index: 1)"
        //   GET  /v1/acl/token/self  X-Consul-Token: <SecretID> -> 200, the same AccessorID
        //   PUT  /v1/kv/tcae/hello "logged in" (text/plain), then GET ...?raw, then DELETE -> true, the value, true
        // Take the SecretID from the replayed bootstrap response, as a client
        // would, and send it as X-Consul-Token. The reset index is collapsed.
        spec.it("bootstraps the ACL system, which is how a token is first minted") callback {
            let c: *docker.Container = null
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                c2, err = consul.run(IMAGE) { config_string(API_CONFIG) }
                testing.cleanup_container(c2)
                spec.assert_ok(err, "consul starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                c = c2
                await_leader(c)
                // ACL setup follows the election by a moment: wait until the
                // anonymous token answers "ACL not found" (not "ACL support
                // disabled" or a 500) before recording, so no poll is on the tape.
                tries = 0
                ready = 0
                while tries < 100 && ready == 0 {
                    s0, b0, e0 = http_send("GET", "${agent_url(c)}/v1/acl/token/self", "", "application/json", "")
                    if e0 == "" && s0 == 403 && string.contains(b0, "ACL not found") == 1 { ready = 1 }
                    tries = tries + 1
                    if ready == 0 { sleep(100) }
                }
                spec.assert_eq(ready, 1, "the ACL system is ready")
            }
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("consul", "bootstraps_the_acl_system", agent_url(c))
            api = base
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "status/leader", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "status/leader needs no token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, ":8300", "the leader is a server RPC address")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "acl/token/self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "no token yet: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "ACL not found", "ACL not found")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "kv/tcae/hello", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "the anonymous token may not read: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "anonymous token lacks permission 'key:read'", "the anonymous token lacks key:read")
            st, b = anonymous("PUT", "acl/bootstrap", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "bootstrap: ${b}")
            secret = jstr(b, "SecretID")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(secret) > 0, "a SecretID")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "ID"), secret, "ID is the SecretID too")
            accessor = jstr(b, "AccessorID")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(accessor) > 0, "an AccessorID")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Policies.0.Name"), "global-management", "the global-management policy")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Description"), "Bootstrap Token (Global Management)", "its description")
            st, b = anonymous("PUT", "acl/bootstrap", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "a second bootstrap is refused: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "ACL bootstrap no longer allowed", "no longer allowed")
            st, b = cv_as(secret, "GET", "acl/token/self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "token/self with the new token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "AccessorID"), accessor, "the same token")
            tok = secret
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/hello", "logged in")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the token writes: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "true")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/hello?raw", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the token reads: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "logged in", "the value")
            st, b = cv("DELETE", "kv/tcae/hello", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the token deletes: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: nobody, or somebody Consul does not know. The first six send
        // no token.
        //   GET /v1/status/leader      -> 200 (public)
        //   GET /v1/catalog/datacenters -> 200 ["dc1"] (public)
        //   GET /v1/catalog/nodes      -> 200 [] (lists are FILTERED to what the token may see, not refused)
        //   GET /v1/kv/tcae/private    -> 403 "Permission denied: anonymous token lacks permission 'key:read' ..."
        //   PUT /v1/kv/tcae/private    -> 403 "... 'key:write' ..."
        //   GET /v1/acl/tokens         -> 403 "Permission denied: anonymous token lacks permission 'acl:read' ..."
        //   GET /v1/kv/tcae/private  X-Consul-Token: not-a-token -> 403 "token does not exist: ACL not found"
        //        (the tape's header is X_CONSUL_TOKEN_1 and replay matches on presence, so replay
        //        cannot tell this from a good token, only Consul could)
        spec.it("refuses an anonymous or unknown token") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("refuses_an_anonymous_or_unknown_token", [])
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "status/leader", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "status/leader is public: ${b}")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "catalog/datacenters", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "datacenters are public: ${b}")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "catalog/nodes", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "nodes are filtered, not refused: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "[]", "an empty list")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "kv/tcae/private", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "reading needs a token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Permission denied", "permission denied")
            st, b = anonymous("PUT", "kv/tcae/private", "x")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "writing needs a token: ${b}")
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "acl/tokens", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "listing tokens needs a token: ${b}")
            st, b = cv_as("not-a-token", "GET", "kv/tcae/private", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "a made-up token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "ACL not found", "ACL not found")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- the cluster ---------------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: one server node named tcae-node, datacenter dc1.
        //   GET /v1/status/leader           -> 200 "127.0.0.1:8300"
        //   GET /v1/status/peers            -> 200 ["127.0.0.1:8300"]
        //   GET /v1/catalog/datacenters     -> 200 ["dc1"]
        //   GET /v1/catalog/nodes           -> 200 [{"ID":{{uuid-1}},"Node":"tcae-node","Address":"127.0.0.1","Datacenter":"dc1",...}]
        //   GET /v1/catalog/node/tcae-node  -> 200 {"Node":{..},"Services":{"consul":{"ID":"consul","Service":"consul","Port":8300,..}}}
        //   GET /v1/catalog/services        -> 200 {"consul":[]}
        //   GET /v1/agent/members           -> 200 [{"Name":"tcae-node","Addr":"127.0.0.1","Port":8301,"Status":1,
        //        "Tags":{"role":"consul","dc":"dc1","acls":"1",..}}]
        //   GET /v1/health/node/tcae-node   -> 200 [{"CheckID":"serfHealth","Status":"passing","Output":"Agent alive and reachable",..}]
        spec.it("reports the leader, peers, datacenters, nodes and members") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_the_leader_peers_datacenters_nodes_and_members", [])
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = cv("GET", "status/leader", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "leader: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, ":8300", "a server RPC address")
            st, b = cv("GET", "status/peers", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "peers: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, ":8300", "one peer")
            st, b = cv("GET", "catalog/datacenters", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "datacenters: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0"), "dc1", "dc1")
            st, b = cv("GET", "catalog/nodes", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "nodes: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Node"), "tcae-node", "the node")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Datacenter"), "dc1", "its datacenter")
            st, b = cv("GET", "catalog/node/tcae-node", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "node: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Services.consul.Service"), "consul", "it runs the consul service")
            st, b = cv("GET", "catalog/services", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "services: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"consul\"", "consul")
            st, b = cv("GET", "agent/members", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "members: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Name"), "tcae-node", "the member")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Tags.role"), "consul", "a server")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Tags.acls"), "1", "with ACLs")
            st, b = cv("GET", "health/node/tcae-node", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "health of the node: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.CheckID"), "serfHealth", "the serf check")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Status"), "passing", "passing")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- KV ------------------------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: keys under tcae/kv/. Values are text/plain bodies; a read
        // returns base64 in JSON, or the raw bytes with ?raw.
        //   PUT    /v1/kv/tcae/kv/a "hello" -> 200 "true\n"
        //   GET    /v1/kv/tcae/kv/a -> 200 [{"LockIndex":0,"Key":"tcae/kv/a","Flags":0,"Value":"aGVsbG8=","CreateIndex":1,"ModifyIndex":1}]
        //   GET    /v1/kv/tcae/kv/a?raw -> 200 "hello" (application/octet-stream)
        //   PUT    /v1/kv/tcae/kv/a?flags=42 "updated" -> true; GET -> Flags 42, Value "dXBkYXRlZA=="
        //   PUT    /v1/kv/tcae/kv/b {"j":1} and PUT /v1/kv/tcae/kv/sub/c "c" -> true
        //   GET    /v1/kv/tcae/kv?keys -> 200 ["tcae/kv/a","tcae/kv/b","tcae/kv/sub/c"] (sorted)
        //   GET    /v1/kv/tcae/kv/?keys&separator=/ -> 200 ["tcae/kv/a","tcae/kv/b","tcae/kv/sub/"]
        //   GET    /v1/kv/tcae/kv?recurse -> 200 three entries, in key order
        //   GET    /v1/kv/tcae/kv/missing -> 404 (empty body)
        //   DELETE /v1/kv/tcae/kv/b -> true ; DELETE /v1/kv/tcae/kv?recurse -> true ; GET /v1/kv/tcae/kv/a -> 404
        spec.it("puts, gets, lists and deletes keys") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("kv_puts_gets_lists_and_deletes_keys", ["DELETE kv/tcae/kv?recurse"])
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/kv/a", "hello")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "put: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "true")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/kv/a", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Key"), "tcae/kv/a", "the key")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Value"), "aGVsbG8=", "the value, base64")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/kv/a?raw", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "raw: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "hello", "the raw value")
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/kv/a?flags=42", "updated")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "put with flags: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/kv/a", "")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Flags\": 42", "the flags")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Value"), "dXBkYXRlZA==", "the new value")
            kv_put("kv/tcae/kv/b", "{\"j\":1}")
            kv_put("kv/tcae/kv/sub/c", "c")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/kv?keys", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "keys: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0"), "tcae/kv/a", "first key")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "2"), "tcae/kv/sub/c", "third key")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/kv/?keys&separator=/", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "keys with a separator: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "2"), "tcae/kv/sub/", "a folder")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/kv?recurse", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "recurse: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "1.Key"), "tcae/kv/b", "second entry")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "2.Key"), "tcae/kv/sub/c", "third entry")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/kv/missing", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a key that is not there: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("DELETE", "kv/tcae/kv/b", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("DELETE", "kv/tcae/kv?recurse", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete recurse: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/kv/a", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "gone: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: check-and-set on tcae/cas. An index is opaque (see the
        // header): read it from the key's ModifyIndex and send it back as
        // ?cas=<it>; on the tape it is 1 throughout. cas=0 means "only if absent".
        //   PUT    /v1/kv/tcae/cas?cas=0 "first"  -> true  (created)
        //   PUT    /v1/kv/tcae/cas?cas=0 "again"  -> false (it exists)
        //   GET    /v1/kv/tcae/cas                -> ModifyIndex (A)
        //   PUT    /v1/kv/tcae/cas?cas=A "second" -> true
        //   PUT    /v1/kv/tcae/cas?cas=A "stale"  -> false (A is now stale)
        //   DELETE /v1/kv/tcae/cas?cas=A          -> false (stale)
        //   GET    /v1/kv/tcae/cas                -> the new ModifyIndex (B), value "second"
        //   DELETE /v1/kv/tcae/cas?cas=B          -> true
        //   GET    /v1/kv/tcae/cas                -> 404
        spec.it("updates and deletes with check-and-set") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("kv_updates_and_deletes_with_check_and_set", ["DELETE kv/tcae/cas"])
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/cas?cas=0", "first")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "cas=0 creates: ${st}")
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/cas?cas=0", "again")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "false\n", "cas=0 on an existing key is refused: ${st}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/cas", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get: ${b}")
            idx = num_after(b, "\"ModifyIndex\": ")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(idx) > 0, "a ModifyIndex")
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/cas?cas=${idx}", "second")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "cas with the current index: ${st}")
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/cas?cas=${idx}", "stale")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "false\n", "cas with a stale index: ${st}")
            st, b = cv("DELETE", "kv/tcae/cas?cas=${idx}", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "false\n", "delete with a stale index: ${st}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/cas", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Value"), "c2Vjb25k", "the value is still the second one (base64)")
            idx2 = num_after(b, "\"ModifyIndex\": ")
            st, b = cv("DELETE", "kv/tcae/cas?cas=${idx2}", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "delete with the current index: ${st}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/cas", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "gone: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: a transaction applies all its operations or none. Values
        // are base64 ("dmFsMQ==" is "val1"). Indexes are opaque.
        //   PUT /v1/txn [{"KV":{"Verb":"set","Key":"tcae/txn/a","Value":"dmFsMQ=="}},
        //                {"KV":{"Verb":"get","Key":"tcae/txn/a"}},
        //                {"KV":{"Verb":"cas","Key":"tcae/txn/b","Value":"dmFsMg==","Index":0}}]
        //        -> 200 {"Results":[three KV results],"Errors":null}
        //   PUT /v1/txn [{"KV":{"Verb":"set","Key":"tcae/txn/c","Value":"eA=="}},
        //                {"KV":{"Verb":"cas","Key":"tcae/txn/a","Value":"eQ==","Index":<stale>}}]
        //        -> 409 {"Results":null,"Errors":[{"OpIndex":1,"What":"failed to set key \"tcae/txn/a\", index is stale"}]}
        //   GET /v1/kv/tcae/txn/c -> 404 (the first op was rolled back)
        //   PUT /v1/txn [{"KV":{"Verb":"delete-tree","Key":"tcae/txn/"}}] -> 200
        //   GET /v1/kv/tcae/txn?keys -> 404
        spec.it("applies a transaction atomically") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("applies_a_transaction_atomically", ["DELETE kv/tcae/txn?recurse"])
            if ok == 0 { return }
            ops1 = "[{\"KV\":{\"Verb\":\"set\",\"Key\":\"tcae/txn/a\",\"Value\":\"dmFsMQ==\"}},{\"KV\":{\"Verb\":\"get\",\"Key\":\"tcae/txn/a\"}},{\"KV\":{\"Verb\":\"cas\",\"Key\":\"tcae/txn/b\",\"Value\":\"dmFsMg==\",\"Index\":0}}]"
            st, b = cv("PUT", "txn", ops1)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "txn: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Results.1.KV.Key"), "tcae/txn/a", "the get result")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Results.1.KV.Value"), "dmFsMQ==", "reads its own write")
            idx = num_after(b, "\"ModifyIndex\": ")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(idx) > 0, "an index")
            // make idx stale: a is rewritten outside the transaction
            kv_put("kv/tcae/txn/a", "changed")
            ops2 = "[{\"KV\":{\"Verb\":\"set\",\"Key\":\"tcae/txn/c\",\"Value\":\"eA==\"}},{\"KV\":{\"Verb\":\"cas\",\"Key\":\"tcae/txn/a\",\"Value\":\"eQ==\",\"Index\":${idx}}}]"
            st, b = cv("PUT", "txn", ops2)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 409, "a stale cas fails the whole transaction: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "index is stale", "index is stale")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/txn/c", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "the set before the failure was rolled back: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "txn", "[{\"KV\":{\"Verb\":\"delete-tree\",\"Key\":\"tcae/txn/\"}}]")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete-tree: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/txn?keys", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "nothing left: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- sessions and locks ----------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: two sessions contend for the lock on tcae/lock. Session
        // ids are uuids ({{uuid-N}}), sent back in ?acquire= and ?release=.
        //   PUT /v1/session/create {"Name":"tcae-holder","TTL":"60s","Behavior":"release","LockDelay":"0s"} -> 200 {"ID":..}
        //   PUT /v1/session/create {"Name":"tcae-waiter","TTL":"60s","Behavior":"delete","LockDelay":"0s"} -> 200 {"ID":..}
        //   GET /v1/session/info/<holder> -> 200 [{"Name":"tcae-holder","Node":"tcae-node","Behavior":"release","TTL":"60s",
        //        "NodeChecks":["serfHealth"],..}]
        //   PUT /v1/kv/tcae/lock?acquire=<holder> "holder" -> true ; PUT ...?acquire=<waiter> "waiter" -> false
        //   GET /v1/kv/tcae/lock -> [{"LockIndex":1,"Session":<holder>,..}]
        //   PUT /v1/session/renew/<holder> -> 200 [the session]
        //   PUT /v1/kv/tcae/lock?release=<holder> "x" -> true ; GET -> no Session, LockIndex 1
        //   PUT /v1/kv/tcae/lock?acquire=<waiter> "waiter" -> true ; GET -> Session <waiter>, LockIndex 2
        //   PUT /v1/session/destroy/<waiter> -> true ; GET /v1/kv/tcae/lock -> 404 (behavior "delete" removed the key)
        //   PUT /v1/session/destroy/<holder> -> true ; GET /v1/session/info/<holder> -> 200 []
        spec.it("holds, contends for and releases a lock with sessions") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("sessions_hold_contend_for_and_release_a_lock", ["DELETE kv/tcae/lock"])
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = cv("PUT", "session/create", "{\"Name\":\"tcae-holder\",\"TTL\":\"60s\",\"Behavior\":\"release\",\"LockDelay\":\"0s\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create holder: ${b}")
            holder = jstr(b, "ID")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(holder) > 0, "a session id")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "session/create", "{\"Name\":\"tcae-waiter\",\"TTL\":\"60s\",\"Behavior\":\"delete\",\"LockDelay\":\"0s\"}")
            waiter = jstr(b, "ID")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(waiter) > 0, "another session id")
            st, b = cv("GET", "session/info/${holder}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "info: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Name"), "tcae-holder", "its name")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Behavior"), "release", "its behavior")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.TTL"), "60s", "its TTL")
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/lock?acquire=${holder}", "holder")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "the holder takes the lock: ${st}")
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/lock?acquire=${waiter}", "waiter")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "false\n", "the waiter cannot: ${st}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/lock", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Session"), holder, "held by the holder")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"LockIndex\": 1", "first acquisition")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "session/renew/${holder}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "renew: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.ID"), holder, "the same session")
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/lock?release=${holder}", "x")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "release: ${st}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/lock", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Session"), "", "no holder now")
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/lock?acquire=${waiter}", "waiter")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "the waiter takes it: ${st}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/lock", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Session"), waiter, "held by the waiter")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"LockIndex\": 2", "second acquisition")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "session/destroy/${waiter}", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "destroy the waiter: ${st}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/lock", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "its key went with it (behavior delete): ${b}")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "session/destroy/${holder}", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "destroy the holder: ${st}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "session/info/${holder}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "info after destroy: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "[]", "no such session")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- services, checks and the catalog ----------------------------------

        // PORTING: an agent service with a TTL check.
        //   PUT /v1/agent/service/register {"ID":"web-1","Name":"web","Tags":["v1","tcae"],"Port":8080,"Address":"10.0.0.5",
        //        "Meta":{"owner":"tcae"},"Check":{"CheckID":"web-1-ttl","Name":"web ttl","TTL":"60s"}} -> 200 (empty body)
        //   GET /v1/agent/services -> 200 {"web-1":{"ID":"web-1","Service":"web","Tags":["v1","tcae"],..,"Port":8080,..}}
        //   GET /v1/agent/checks   -> 200 {"web-1-ttl":{"Status":"critical","Type":"ttl",..}} (a TTL check starts critical)
        //   GET /v1/agent/health/service/id/web-1 -> 503 (critical) with AggregatedStatus "critical"
        //   PUT /v1/agent/check/pass/web-1-ttl?note=ok -> 200 ; the same GET -> 200, AggregatedStatus "passing"
        //   GET /v1/health/service/web?passing -> 200, one entry whose Checks include web-1-ttl with Output "ok"
        //   GET /v1/catalog/service/web -> 200 one entry: ServiceID "web-1", ServicePort 8080, Node "tcae-node"
        //   PUT /v1/agent/check/warn/web-1-ttl?note=slow -> 200 ; GET .../agent/health/service/name/web -> 429 "warning"
        //   GET /v1/health/service/web?passing -> 200 [] (nothing passing)
        //   PUT /v1/agent/check/fail/web-1-ttl?note=down -> 200 ; GET /v1/health/state/critical -> includes web-1-ttl
        //   PUT /v1/agent/service/deregister/web-1 -> 200 ; GET /v1/agent/services -> 200 {}
        //   PUT /v1/agent/service/deregister/web-1 -> 404 "Unknown service ID \"web-1\". Ensure that the service ID is passed, not the service name."
        spec.it("registers a service with a TTL check and follows its health") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("registers_a_service_with_a_ttl_check_and_follows_its_health", ["PUT agent/service/deregister/web-1"])
            if ok == 0 { return }
            reg = "{\"ID\":\"web-1\",\"Name\":\"web\",\"Tags\":[\"v1\",\"tcae\"],\"Port\":8080,\"Address\":\"10.0.0.5\",\"Meta\":{\"owner\":\"tcae\"},\"Check\":{\"CheckID\":\"web-1-ttl\",\"Name\":\"web ttl\",\"TTL\":\"60s\"}}"
            st, b = cv("PUT", "agent/service/register", reg)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "register: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "agent/services", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "services: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "web-1.Service"), "web", "the service")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "web-1.Tags.1"), "tcae", "its tags")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "web-1.Meta.owner"), "tcae", "its meta")
            st, b = cv("GET", "agent/checks", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "checks: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "web-1-ttl.Status"), "critical", "a TTL check starts critical")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "web-1-ttl.Type"), "ttl", "a ttl check")
            st, b = cv("GET", "agent/health/service/id/web-1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 503, "critical is 503: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "AggregatedStatus"), "critical", "critical")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "agent/check/pass/web-1-ttl?note=ok", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "pass: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "agent/health/service/id/web-1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "passing is 200: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "AggregatedStatus"), "passing", "passing")
            st, b = cv("GET", "health/service/web?passing", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "health/service passing: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Service.ID"), "web-1", "the service")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Output\": \"ok\"", "the note is the check's output")
            st, b = cv("GET", "catalog/service/web", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "catalog: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.ServiceID"), "web-1", "ServiceID")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Node"), "tcae-node", "on the node")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "agent/check/warn/web-1-ttl?note=slow", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "warn: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "agent/health/service/name/web", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 429, "warning is 429: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.AggregatedStatus"), "warning", "warning")
            st, b = cv("GET", "health/service/web?passing", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "nothing passes: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "[]", "an empty list")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "agent/check/fail/web-1-ttl?note=down", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "fail: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "health/state/critical", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "critical checks: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"CheckID\": \"web-1-ttl\"", "ours is among them")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "agent/service/deregister/web-1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "deregister: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "agent/services", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(string.replace_all(string.replace_all(b, " ", ""), "\n", ""), "{}", "no services left")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "agent/service/deregister/web-1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "deregistering twice: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Unknown service ID \"web-1\"", "unknown service id")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: a service on a node that runs no agent, registered through
        // the catalog.
        //   PUT /v1/catalog/register {"Node":"ext-node","Address":"192.168.1.10",
        //        "Service":{"ID":"db-1","Service":"db","Port":5432,"Tags":["primary"]}} -> 200 "true\n"
        //   GET /v1/catalog/nodes -> 200, two nodes in name order: ext-node (ID "") and tcae-node
        //   GET /v1/catalog/node/ext-node -> 200 {"Node":{..,"Address":"192.168.1.10"},"Services":{"db-1":{..,"Port":5432}}}
        //   GET /v1/catalog/service/db -> 200 one entry: Node "ext-node", ServiceTags ["primary"]
        //   PUT /v1/catalog/deregister {"Node":"ext-node"} -> 200 "true\n"
        //   GET /v1/catalog/node/ext-node -> 200 "null"
        spec.it("registers an external node and service in the catalog") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("registers_an_external_node_and_service_in_the_catalog", ["PUT catalog/deregister"])
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = cv("PUT", "catalog/register", "{\"Node\":\"ext-node\",\"Address\":\"192.168.1.10\",\"Service\":{\"ID\":\"db-1\",\"Service\":\"db\",\"Port\":5432,\"Tags\":[\"primary\"]}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "register: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "true")
            st, b = cv("GET", "catalog/nodes", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "nodes: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Node"), "ext-node", "first in name order")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "1.Node"), "tcae-node", "then the agent's node")
            st, b = cv("GET", "catalog/node/ext-node", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "node: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Node.Address"), "192.168.1.10", "its address")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Services.db-1.Service"), "db", "its service")
            st, b = cv("GET", "catalog/service/db", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "service: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Node"), "ext-node", "on the external node")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.ServiceTags.0"), "primary", "tagged")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "catalog/deregister", "{\"Node\":\"ext-node\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "deregister: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "catalog/node/ext-node", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the node after: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(string.trim(b), "null", "gone")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- ACL policies and tokens -----------------------------------------

        // PORTING: a policy and a limited token made with the management token
        // (X_CONSUL_TOKEN_1); the limited token's own requests carry its
        // SecretID (X_CONSUL_TOKEN_2). Policy and accessor ids are {{uuid-N}}.
        //   PUT /v1/acl/policy {"Name":"tcae-reader","Description":"read tcae keys","Rules":"key_prefix \"tcae/\" { policy = \"read\" }"}
        //        -> 200 {"ID":{{uuid-1}},"Name":"tcae-reader",..,"Rules":..,"Hash":..}
        //   GET /v1/acl/policy/<id> -> 200 ; GET /v1/acl/policy/name/tcae-reader -> 200, the same
        //   PUT /v1/acl/policy/<id> {..,"Description":"read tcae keys (updated)",..} -> 200
        //   GET /v1/acl/policies -> 200 three: builtin/global-read-only, global-management, tcae-reader (by name)
        //   PUT /v1/acl/token {"Description":"tcae reader","Policies":[{"Name":"tcae-reader"}]}
        //        -> 200 AccessorID {{uuid-2}}, SecretID X_CONSUL_TOKEN_2
        //   GET /v1/acl/token/<accessor> -> 200 ; GET /v1/acl/token/self (reader) -> 200, the same AccessorID
        //   (reader) GET /v1/kv/tcae/x -> 404 (allowed, absent); PUT /v1/kv/tcae/x -> 403 "Permission denied: token with
        //        AccessorID '{{uuid-2}}' lacks permission 'key:write' on "tcae/x""; GET /v1/kv/other/x -> 403 ; GET /v1/acl/tokens -> 403
        //   DELETE /v1/acl/token/<accessor> -> 200 true ; (reader) GET /v1/acl/token/self -> 403 "ACL not found"
        //   DELETE /v1/acl/policy/<id> -> 200 true ; GET /v1/acl/policy/<id> -> 404 "Requested policy does not exist: ACL not found"
        spec.it("manages ACL policies and tokens, and enforces them") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("manages_acl_policies_and_tokens_and_enforces_them", [])
            if ok == 0 { return }
            rules = "key_prefix 'tcae/' { policy = 'read' }"
            st, b = cv("PUT", "acl/policy", "{\"Name\":\"tcae-reader\",\"Description\":\"read tcae keys\",\"Rules\":\"${hcl(rules)}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create the policy: ${b}")
            pid = jstr(b, "ID")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(pid) > 0, "a policy id")
            st, b = cv("GET", "acl/policy/${pid}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read by id: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Rules"), string.replace_all(rules, "'", "\""), "the rules as written")
            st, b = cv("GET", "acl/policy/name/tcae-reader", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read by name: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "ID"), pid, "the same policy")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "acl/policy/${pid}", "{\"Name\":\"tcae-reader\",\"Description\":\"read tcae keys (updated)\",\"Rules\":\"${hcl(rules)}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "update: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Description"), "read tcae keys (updated)", "updated")
            st, b = cv("GET", "acl/policies", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0.Name"), "builtin/global-read-only", "first by name")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "2.Name"), "tcae-reader", "ours last")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "acl/token", "{\"Description\":\"tcae reader\",\"Policies\":[{\"Name\":\"tcae-reader\"}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create the token: ${b}")
            accessor = jstr(b, "AccessorID")
            reader = jstr(b, "SecretID")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(accessor) > 0, "an accessor")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(reader) > 0, "a secret")
            st, b = cv("GET", "acl/token/${accessor}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "read the token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Policies.0.Name"), "tcae-reader", "its policy")
            st, b = cv_as(reader, "GET", "acl/token/self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "token/self as the reader: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "AccessorID"), accessor, "the reader")
            st, b = cv_as(reader, "GET", "kv/tcae/x", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "the reader may read tcae/: ${b}")
            st, b, werr = http_send("PUT", "${api}/v1/kv/tcae/x", reader, "text/plain", "v")
            spec.assert_ok(werr, "PUT kv/tcae/x as the reader")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "the reader may not write: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "lacks permission 'key:write'", "key:write")
            st, b = cv_as(reader, "GET", "kv/other/x", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "nor read elsewhere: ${b}")
            st, b = cv_as(reader, "GET", "acl/tokens", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "nor list tokens: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("DELETE", "acl/token/${accessor}", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "delete the token: ${st}")
            st, b = cv_as(reader, "GET", "acl/token/self", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 403, "a deleted token is gone: ${b}")
            st, b = cv("DELETE", "acl/policy/${pid}", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "true\n", "delete the policy: ${st}")
            st, b = cv("GET", "acl/policy/${pid}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "the policy is gone: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Requested policy does not exist", "does not exist")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // ---- errors -------------------------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: the representative error statuses, logged in. Consul's
        // errors are plain text. (403 is shown by the token cases.)
        //   PUT    /v1/kv/tcae/err?flags=abc "v"      -> 500 "strconv.ParseUint: parsing \"abc\": invalid syntax"
        //   GET    /v1/kv/tcae/err?index=abc          -> 400 "Invalid index"
        //   PUT    /v1/catalog/register {bad          -> 400 "Request decode failed: invalid character 'b' looking for ..."
        //   PUT    /v1/agent/check/pass/nosuch        -> 404 "Unknown check ID \"nosuch\". Ensure that the check ID is passed, not the check name."
        //   GET    /v1/nosuch                         -> 404 "Invalid URL path: not a recognized HTTP API endpoint"
        //   DELETE /v1/status/leader                  -> 405 "method DELETE not allowed"
        //   PUT    /v1/session/create {"TTL":"1s"}    -> 500 "Invalid Session TTL '1000000000', must be between [10s=24h0m0s]"
        //   PUT    /v1/acl/token {"Policies":[{"Name":"nosuch"}]} -> 500 "No such ACL policy with name \"nosuch\""
        //   GET    /v1/acl/policy/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009 -> 404 "Requested policy does not exist: ACL not found"
        spec.it("answers the representative error statuses") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("answers_the_representative_error_statuses", [])
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = kv_put("kv/tcae/err?flags=abc", "v")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 500, "flags that are not a number (Consul answers 500): ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "invalid syntax", "invalid syntax")
            st, b = cv("GET", "kv/tcae/err?index=abc", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "an index that is not a number: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Invalid index", "Invalid index")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "catalog/register", "{bad")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a body that is not JSON: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Request decode failed", "Request decode failed")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "agent/check/pass/nosuch", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a check that does not exist: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Unknown check ID", "Unknown check ID")
            st, b = cv("GET", "nosuch", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a path that is no endpoint: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "not a recognized HTTP API endpoint", "not a recognized endpoint")
            st, b = cv("DELETE", "status/leader", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 405, "the wrong method: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "method DELETE not allowed", "method DELETE not allowed")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "session/create", "{\"TTL\":\"1s\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 500, "a session TTL below the minimum (Consul answers 500): ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Invalid Session TTL", "Invalid Session TTL")
            st, b = cv("PUT", "acl/token", "{\"Policies\":[{\"Name\":\"nosuch\"}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 500, "a token for a policy that does not exist (Consul answers 500): ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "No such ACL policy", "No such ACL policy")
            st, b = cv("GET", "acl/policy/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a policy id that does not exist: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Requested policy does not exist", "does not exist")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

    }

    if shared_container != null {
        e = tc.terminate(shared_container as *docker.Container)
        if e != "" { println("consul: removing the shared container: ${e}") }
    }
    return spec.run_summary(fw)
}
